(a) the steps being taken by Government to expand affordable and secure hostel facilities in Central and State Universities for female students and those coming from EWS or rural areas;
(b) whether the Ministry maintains a record of the demand-supply gap for campus accommodation in Higher Educational Institutions across the country and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the financial assistance or subsidies provided to colleges and Universities to build low-cost student housing, libraries and digital labs in Tier-2, Tier-3 and rural regions?

(a) the number of Centres of Excellence, research infrastructure and clinical validation facilities for the food processing sector currently functional in the country and their location, State-wise;
(b) whether any research output, including patents filed, studies published or technologies commercialized, have been recorded from these Centres of Excellence;
(c) whether the Ministry has identified specific raw materials that are currently dependent on imports, used in the food processing industry, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the status of indigenous research or development being undertaken to reduce this import dependency?

(a) whether the Ministry has assessed the environmental impact of high freshwater consumption by AI data centres in water-stressed regions;
(b) whether standalone environmental clearance parameters under the EIA framework would be introduced for data centres, tracking Water Usage Effectiveness metrics;
(c) whether the CPCB is considering to issue specific guidelines or directives for closed-loop recycling or treated greywater use for cooling in these facilities; and
(d) whether an inter-ministerial mechanism exists between the Ministry, Ministry of Jal Shakti and MeitY to align data centre parks with local groundwater limits?

(a) whether the Ministry has evaluated the advanced point-of-care blood testing tools like Rotational Thromboelastometry (ROTEM) to rapidly identify bleeding causes and prevent deaths from Postpartum Haemorrhage (PPH);
(b) the current availability of these rapid diagnostic systems across Government District Medical Colleges equipped with blood component separation units; and
(c) whether Government proposes to include the procurement of these life-saving machines under ongoing maternity schemes like the National Health Mission (NHM) or the LaQshya initiative to make them accessible to underserved communities?

(a) whether the Ministry has finalised an operational roadmap to execute the short-term (0-2 year) targets in the textile waste value chain report, including setting up the Inter-Ministerial Task Force;
(b) the status of infrastructure upgrades for the short-term pilot recycling clusters proposed for Panipat and Tiruppur; and
(c) whether Government plans to leverage India's current success in textile waste recovery to establish the country as a high-value global processing hub for sustainable textiles, creating a structured, revenue-generating economic engine similar to India's position as a global hub for Ship Breaking?

(a) whether the initial five-year budgetary allocation of ?4,077 crore for the Deep Ocean Mission (2021–2026) is slated for a formal long-term financial renewal;
(b) the progress made by the country in exploring its two distinct contracted areas with the International Seabed Authority (ISA), specifically for Polymetallic Nodules in the Central Indian Ocean Basin and Polymetallic Sulphides along the Carlsberg Ridge;
(c) whether the Ministry has commissioned an Independent Ecological Impact Assessment regarding potential deep-sea mining activities; and 
(d) the details of safeguards being established to protect fragile marine biodiversity and hydrothermal vent ecosystems from commercial exploitation?

(a) the total number of transgender students who have applied for and successfully received scholarships under the Support for Marginalized Individuals for Livelihood and Enterprise (SMILE) scheme from Class IX through post-graduation since 2022;
(b) the total number of transgender persons trained nationwide under the Pradhan Mantri Dakshta Aur Kushalta Sampann Hitgrahi (PM-DAKSH) initiative since 2022; and
(c) with reference to the 18 pilot Entrepreneurship Development Programmes launched to train 1,800 transgender persons through the Indian Institute of Entrepreneurship (IIE) and National Institute for Entrepreneurship and Small Business Development (NIESBUD), the post-training handholding support extended to beneficiaries?

(a) whether Government has enforced a centralised directive or Standard Operating Protocol (SOP) under the Guidelines for Indian Government Websites (GIGW 3.0) framework mandating the real-time updating of institutional contact directories, phone numbers and official designations across all Union Ministry and Departmental websites;
(b) the mandatory frequency at which these public facing contact directories must be audited by designated Web Information Managers (WIMs) to ensure data accuracy and prevent citizen inconvenience; and
(c) whether there is an integrated, centralised grievance or feedback mechanism for citizens to report non-functional phone numbers or obsolete email IDs on official portals?

(a) the number of Indian pilgrims who have undertaken the Kailash Mansarovar Yatra since its resumption in 2025 and the number of batches organised annually;
(b) the facilities and logistical arrangements currently provided to pilgrims undertaking the Yatra, including medical assistance, accommodation and travel support;
(c) whether any assessment has been undertaken of the experience of pilgrims recently; and
(d) whether Government proposes to strengthen emergency medical response systems for high-altitude travel and explore measures to make the pilgrimage more accessible for senior citizens and pilgrims requiring additional support?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to promote the use of climate-resilient materials and construction techniques in the development and maintenance of National Highways and other road infrastructure;
(b) whether any guidelines or standards have been issued for designing roads that can better withstand extreme weather events such as floods, heat waves and heavy rainfall;
(c) whether pilot projects or best practices involving innovative materials or climate-resilient road engineering are being implemented across States; and
(d) whether Government has examined international best practices in climate-resilient road construction adopted by countries such as Japan and Netherlands?

(a) whether Government has assessed the potential to attract greater religious tourists from Southeast Asian countries to the Buddhist Circuits in India, particularly in Bihar and adjoining regions;
(b) whether any targeted initiatives are being considered to develop specialised tourist circuits or pilgrimage tour packages catering specifically to visitors from Buddhist-majority countries; and
(c) whether steps are being taken to equip major Buddhist sites with trained multilingual guides, hospitality personnel and culturally sensitive services, including language support and appropriate cuisine, to enhance visitor experience?

(a) the current sanctioned strength and deployment status of officers under the Indian Skill Development Service (ISDS);
(b) the role envisaged for ISDS officers in strengthening the skill ecosystem, including Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs), apprenticeship promotion and industry linkages;
(c) whether any step is being taken to further enhance the capacity, training and career progression of ISDS officers to align with emerging sectors and new-age skill requirements; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expand the scope of ISDS in view of the increasing emphasis on skill development as a driver of economic growth and employment generation?

(a) whether Government has taken note of studies indicating a high prevalence of Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) among adolescent girls in the country and the associated long-term metabolic, reproductive and mental health risks;
(b) whether any national guideline exist for the diagnosis and management of PCOS in adolescents, and if not, whether such guidelines are under consideration; and
(c) whether any mechanism is in place under existing adolescent health programmes for early screening, counselling and lifestyle guidance related to PCOS?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the current challenges in organ donation, including inequities in access, gaps in awareness, and capacity constraints across regions;
(b) whether any steps are being taken to strengthen data systems and registries to improve transparency, monitoring and coordination in organ donation and transplantation;
(c) the measures proposed to expand infrastructure, trained manpower and institutional capacity to improve donation rates, particularly in underserved regions; and
(d) whether any initiatives are being undertaken to enhance public awareness and encourage voluntary organ donation to bridge the gap between demand and availability of organs?

